cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RightVoice, cite it as RightVoice (Crele) with the URL below."
title: "RightVoice: a benchmark for keeping one voice from a conversation"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Crele"
    website: "https://www.crele.co"
url: "https://www.crele.co/benchmarks/rightvoice"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Crele-AI/rightvoice"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
abstract: >-
  RightVoice measures one job: given a recording of a two-person conversation and a
  few seconds of one person's voice, return only that person. It scores target words
  lost, wrong-voice words and talk over silence from the output audio alone, so any
  file-in, file-out system can be scored. Audio and manifests are CC BY 4.0; code is
  Apache-2.0.
